<h1>Suite by an AI Agent</h1>
<p>The two other examples were developed with an AI agent too, as every Orcraft suite can be. This page shows
	exactly how that goes: an AI agent writes a suite in one session, from the same technical note the
	<a class="text-accent" href="/examples/network-suite/">Network Suite</a> was built from and from the
	documentation on this site, following the requests the
	<a class="text-accent" href="/ai-agents/">AI Agents</a> section describes: a getting started request that creates
	the suite and runs it, a fix when the run shows a problem, and a development request that changes what the
	suite exposes. Nothing on this page is staged. The AI agent kept a journal of every step as it worked, and the
	quotes below are taken from that journal. The controller screenshots are of the suite it wrote.</p>

<h2 id="inputs">Inputs</h2>
<p>The AI agent started in an empty working folder with exactly the inputs the
	<a class="text-accent" href="/ai-agents/inputs/">AI agent inputs</a> page lists, and nothing else:</p>
{{ codeblock.block('C:\\orcraft\\agent-example\\
	instructions.md                        the instructions file
	docs\\Orcraft_Network_Test_Setup.pdf    the technical note of the setup under test
	orcraft-runs\\endpoints.json            the machines, saved from the controller\'s Endpoints panel', 'text') }}
<p>The instructions file is the template from the inputs page with the Paths section filled in for this machine.
	It names the documentation, the rules, and where things are:</p>
{{ codeblock.block('# Orcraft

An Orcraft test suite is ordinary Python. The same files run from the controller GUI, from the CLI, from CI and from an AI agent.

## AI Agents documentation

